{
  "id": "jsonbored_metagraphed_2432",
  "repo_name": "jsonbored/metagraphed",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/jsonbored/metagraphed",
  "base_commit": "562731ce0c4dd96ff8a77b3fc6f5e76db2e5eb20",
  "pr_number": 2432,
  "issue_number": 2422,
  "issue_title": "feat(api): GET /api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/stake-flow, net staked vs unstaked over a window",
  "issue_body": "## Problem / why it matters\n\nStake is the capital signal in Bittensor, but the registry has no way to ask whether a subnet is gaining or losing stake over time. We serve the raw per-event feed (`/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/events?kind=StakeAdded`) and validator churn (`/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/turnover`), but a consumer who wants \"is capital flowing into this subnet or draining out of it, and by how much?\" has to page every StakeAdded and StakeRemoved row and sum them client-side. Turnover answers who entered or left the validator set; it does not answer how much TAO actually moved. Every capital tracker surfaces a net-flow view, and we already store every input.\n\n## Current state (verified)\n\n- The `account_events` D1 tier stores each stake event with an `amount_tao REAL` column (tao field / 1e9), per `migrations/0009_account_events.sql:21`. StakeAdded and StakeRemoved both carry it (`src/account-events.mjs`, EVENT_INSERT_COLUMNS plus the ingested-kinds set). `observed_at` is the block timestamp in epoch ms, and the tier keeps a rolling ~90-day hot window.\n- `migrations/0024_account_events_kind_index.sql` indexes `account_events (netuid, event_kind, block_number)`, which is exactly the seek a per-subnet, per-kind aggregate needs.\n- `handleSubnetEvents` (`workers/request-handlers/entities.mjs:859`) is the established live-D1, null-safe per-subnet account_events reader (cold store returns 200 empty, never 404); `handleSubnetTurnover` (`entities.mjs:417`) plus the pure `src/turnover.mjs` module are the established compute-and-scorecard pattern.\n- No stake-flow, inflow/outflow, or net-stake endpoint exists anywhere (`src/contracts.mjs`, `workers/api.mjs`).\n\n## Proposed addition\n\n`GET /api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/stake-flow?window=7d|30d|90d` (default 30d), computed live from `account_events`, returning a stake-flow scorecard over the window:\n\n- `total_staked_tao` (sum of StakeAdded amount_tao)\n- `total_unstaked_tao` (sum of StakeRemoved amount_tao)\n- `net_flow_tao` (staked minus unstaked, positive means net inflow)\n- `stake_events` / `unstake_events` (counts)\n- `window` and `netuid` context\n\nAll TAO sums rounded to rao precision (matches the rounding in `src/turnover.mjs`). The windows are 7d/30d/90d because `account_events` keeps a rolling ~90-day hot window, which is exactly the recent-capital-flow signal a flow view answers. Schema-stable: a cold or empty store returns zeroed totals with a 200, never a 404, mirroring the sibling routes.\n\n## Implementation sketch\n\n- New pure module `src/stake-flow.mjs`: `buildStakeFlow(rows, netuid, opts)` (the sums, net, and counts, fully unit-testable) plus `loadSubnetStakeFlow(d1, netuid, opts)`.\n- `handleSubnetStakeFlow` in `workers/request-handlers/entities.mjs`, sibling to `handleSubnetTurnover`, one indexed `GROUP BY event_kind` read over `account_events` (`observed_at >= now - windowDays`) using `idx_account_events_netuid_kind`.\n- A `SUBNET_STAKE_FLOW_PATH_PATTERN` in `workers/config.mjs` (next to `SUBNET_TURNOVER_PATH_PATTERN`) plus edge-cached dispatch in `workers/api.mjs`.\n- Register the live route in `src/contracts.mjs` (artifact plus route), mark it computed (`R2_ONLY_PATTERNS` in `src/artifact-storage.mjs`, `COMPUTED_ARTIFACTS` in `scripts/validate-schemas.mjs`), add a `SubnetStakeFlowArtifact` schema, and regenerate `openapi.json` and types via `npm run build`.\n\nNo new data collection, no new D1 tier, no static artifact. Pure live aggregation over stake events we already ingest, on an index we already ship.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-06-30T18:23:50.000Z",
